This MIT license applies to the code in this repository. Data files in
public/data/ are governed by the licenses of their upstream sources, listed
in src/data/series.json and on the live site at /methods. In summary:

- Voteview / DW-NOMINATE: freely available; project code MIT-licensed; no
  explicit data license.
- FRBSF Fernald TFP: freely available; © FRBSF, no explicit reuse license.
- WID Top 1% Wealth Share: CC BY 4.0.
- Maddison Project Database 2023: CC BY 4.0.
- V-Dem Liberal Democracy Index v16: CC BY-SA 4.0.
- Project Mars (via Our World in Data): OWID chart layer CC BY 4.0;
  underlying Project Mars data Public Domain (Harvard Dataverse).

The seven cycle theories themselves are works of named authors (Khaldun,
Kondratiev, Huntington, Perez, Turchin, Dalio, Strauss & Howe) cited in
src/data/cycles.json. Their texts are not redistributed here; only short
descriptive quotations and editorial summaries appear in the prose pages.

The prose on the live site (the home page, /about, /methods, /colophon, the
poster, and the build journal at docs/how-this-was-made.md) is authored by
David Kooi / Skylark Creations. Reuse with attribution is welcome.
